            <ArticleTitle>[Chilaiditi syndrome--general indications for surgical therapy?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The usually asymptomatic Chilaiditi's syndrome is a rare anomaly which in most cases is detected accidentally by x-rays. We report two unusual cases with incarcerated interpositio coli hepato-diaphragmatica. Differential diagnosis and surgical management are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
